nt researching how to diagnose and treat cancerous cells in an extremely targeted manner. (Graduate Entrance Scholarship and NSERC CGS Masters Scholarship)\nLearn More\nBrooklyn Fedoretz-Maxwell\nBrooklyn is a Chemistry master's student who is researching metalloproteins. (NSERC CGS Masters Scholarship)\nLearn More\nEmmanuel Balogun\nEmmanuel is a Chemistry PhD student researching on fuel cells and how they can be made cheaper and more efficient with environmentally friendly starting materials. (MITACS Research Training Award, Chemistry Graduate fellowship (3), and NSERC Vanier Canada Graduate Scholarship)\nLearn More\nParsa Sojoudi\nParsa is a Chemistry master\u2019s student researching the DNA sequence detection of two different Ginseng species. (Special Graduate Entrance Scholarship)\nLearn More\nAnnabelle Kilham\nAnnabelle is a Chemistry Doctoral student in the Faculty of Science whose research focuses on optimizing nanoparticle catalysts for their use in fuel cells. (Special Graduate Entrance Scholarship & NSERC CGS Masters Scholarship)\nLearn More\nParmissa Randhawa\nParmissa is a Nuclear Medicinal Inorganic Chemistry Doctoral student in the Faculty of Science researching on the development of new pharmaceuticals (radiopharmaceuticals) for cancer that incorporates a radioactive metal atom. (BC Graduate Scholarship)\nLearn More\nFranklin Egemole\nFranklin is a Chemistry PhD student in the Faculty of Science whose research is focused on the design or improvement of systems that will help promote the production of hydrogen as a renewable energy source. (Graduate Dean Entrance Scholarship)\nLearn More\nHimani Sethi\nHimani is a Chemistry master's student whose research is focused on developing inhibitors for carbohydrate processing enzymes in the human body.\nLearn More\nFeatured Research\nStrategies to control the geometry and symmetry around lanthanide centres for tailored luminescence and magnetism\nKarpiuk, T. E. & Leznoff, D. B.\nNat Commun 17, 2845 (2026). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-69445-6\nContact us\nTo learn more about SFU\u2019s Chemistry department, please get in touch:\nE: chemgdin@sfu.ca\nT: (778)-782-3345\nDepartment of Chemistry\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nResearch\nDepartment\nNews & Events\nContact Us\nEDI\nSupport\nContact us\n8888 University Drive\nBurnaby, B.C.\nCanada V5A 1S6\nSafety & Risk\nSFU Maps & Directions\nSFU Admissions\nRoad Report\nGive to SFU\nEmergency Information\nA-Z Directory\nSimon Fraser University respectfully acknowledges the x\u02b7m\u0259\u03b8k\u02b7\u0259y\u0313\u0259m (Musqueam), S\u1e35wx\u0331w\u00fa7mesh \u00daxwumixw (Squamish), s\u0259lilw\u0259ta\u026c (Tsleil-Waututh), q\u0313\u00edc\u0313\u0259y\u0313 (Katzie), k\u02b7ik\u02b7\u0259\u019b\u0313\u0259m (Kwikwetlem), Qayqayt, Kwantlen, Semiahmoo and Tsawwassen peoples on whose unceded traditional territories our three campuses reside.\nTerms & ConditionsPrivacy policy\u00a9 Simon Fraser University\nUndergraduate\nOverview\nProspective Students\nOverview\nDegree Programs\nAdmission & Transferring\nCareers\nFinancial Aid\nCurrent Students\nOverview\nCourses\nAdvising\nFAQs\nForms & Resources\nForms\nProgram Planning\nResources\nUndergraduate Research Opportunities\nChemistry Co-op\nResearch Awards & Scholarships\nOverview\nUndergraduate Research Presentation Award\nCSC Silver Medal Award\nE. J. Wells Chemistry Book Award\nMelanie O'Neill Chemistry Undergraduate Award\nSCI Canada Student Merit Award\nTony Parsad Award in Chemistry\nChemistry Undergraduate Scholarship\nTransCanada Pipelines Research Scholarship\nEvelyn and Leigh Palmer Scholarship\nUndergraduate Research\nGraduate\nOverview\nProspective Students\nOverview\nPrograms\nEligibility & Requirements\nMSc\nPhD\nHow to Apply\nProject Opportunities\nFunding\nCurrent Students\nOverview\nMSc & PhD Program Requirements\nCourses\nSupervisory Committee\nScholarships & Awards\nWestern Deans Agreement\nThesis Defence\nGraduate Caucus\nResearch\nOverview\nResearch Areas\n